From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:27:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Download attachments into memory, with a timeout

download_attachment() creates the destination file and hands it to
whatsmeow's DownloadToFile(). That path fallocate()s the *os.File before
streaming into it. Filesystems without fallocate support (vfat, older
tmpfs) answer EOPNOTSUPP; whatsmeow treats that like a network error and
retries against the next media host, writing into the same, never
truncated file, until the HMAC check fails with "invalid media hmac". The
attachment is lost.

The download also used context.TODO(). It runs synchronously on the
whatsmeow event goroutine through a blocking cgo call, so a stalled media
host blocks event handling, including keep-alives, for as long as the
retries take.

Fetch the media with Download(), which reads into memory and verifies the
HMAC without touching the file system, write the file with os.WriteFile(),
and bound the request to 90 seconds.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 handle_attachment.go | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/handle_attachment.go b/handle_attachment.go
index b462d0f..1163f4b 100644
--- a/handle_attachment.go
+++ b/handle_attachment.go
@@ -139,9 +139,22 @@ func (handler *Handler) handle_attachment(message *waE2E.Message, id string, sou
 
 func (handler *Handler) download_attachment(local_file_path string, message whatsmeow.DownloadableMessage) error {
 	os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(local_file_path), 0o755)
-	file, err := os.Create(local_file_path)
+	// Download to memory then write the file ourselves. whatsmeow's DownloadToFile streams to an
+	// *os.File and unconditionally calls fallocate(2), which some filesystems (tmpfs/vfat) reject
+	// with EOPNOTSUPP; that gets misclassified as a network error, retried across hosts, and the
+	// reused-but-not-truncated file corrupts the payload into an "invalid media hmac" failure.
+	// The in-memory Download() path does io.ReadAll (no fallocate, no *os.File) and verifies the HMAC.
+	//
+	// This runs synchronously on the whatsmeow event goroutine (purple_handle_attachment ->
+	// download_to_templated_destination -> gowhatsapp_go_download_attachment is a blocking cgo call).
+	// context.TODO() has no deadline, so a failing/stalled download could block event handling (and
+	// keep-alive) for minutes. Bound every download so a bad media fetch surfaces as a per-message
+	// error instead.
+	ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 90*time.Second)
+	defer cancel()
+	data, err := handler.client.Download(ctx, message)
 	if err != nil {
 		return err
 	}
-	return handler.client.DownloadToFile(context.TODO(), message, file)
+	return os.WriteFile(local_file_path, data, 0o644)
 }
